Fixed: under --print and --output-format json, stdout now carries only the answer, and tool progress goes to stderr. It's committed (997f8029, on top of the WIP commit 130e3850). Build, the full cargo test run, clippy with -D warnings and the format check all pass.

The fix. I added one helper, write_chrome(s), in src/prompt.rs. It writes to stderr when stdout is reserved for the answer (--print, --output-format json) and to stdout otherwise, with the same bytes as the old print!. All 17 non-answer print sites in the event loop now go through it, including the turn boundary, the ▶ tool line, ✓/✗ results and the Ctrl+C notice. The answer text still goes to stdout exactly as before. I committed this before running any cargo command, as the task required.

Tests (tests/print_stdout_contract.rs). The local stub server can now return a sequence of responses: first a read_file call on a.txt, then the final answer. Four new tests; the existing four are unchanged and still pass:
• `--print with a tool turn: stdout equals the answer exactly (a trailing newline is the only extra allowed) and contains no ▶`.
• --output-format json with a tool turn: stdout parses as exactly one JSON value.
• Both tests also check that ▶ read a.txt appears on stderr, so the tool really ran and its line was moved, not deleted.
• Near-miss: plain `-p (no --print) still prints the progress line on stdout, so the REPL and plain -p` behave as before.

Positive control. In one command I disabled the stderr branch of the helper (marked NEUTERED), ran the tests and restored the file. Exactly the two new stdout-reserve tests failed by name and the rest stayed green. Afterwards there were no NEUTERED markers and no diff to prompt.rs.

Docs. docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md said "Tool-progress lines … still print to stdout today"; that line now says progress goes to stderr and stdout carries only the answer. I also added a Day 212 note under prompt.rs in ARCHITECTURE.md.

Worth knowing:
• With a tool turn, --print output ends without a trailing newline. The test allows either, because whether to add one is a separate product decision.
• `.yoyo/risk_weights.json already had uncommitted changes when I started. The task's git add -A` swept them into the WIP commit.
• **Out of scope, not fixed:** the leading `\n\n` in the collected response text; where it comes from is still unmeasured. I also didn't re-check `print_context_usage` and `print_usage`, which still print to stdout unless quiet mode is on.
